5. CAVEATS
==============================================================================
* Groups and Efficacy are perfectly separated in the data (Group 1: 41/41 PR; Group 2: 0/39 PR,
  22 PD + 17 SD). Groups carries no textual label, so "which group is the treatment arm" is an
  ASSUMPTION, not a fact from the file. The model therefore does NOT filter on Groups and does not
  include it (per protocol: age is the only predictor).
* Consequence: the marginal age slope is confounded with / mixed up with the treatment-group effect
  (Group 1 mean age 54.9 vs Group 2 62.4). p(65) is a cohort-level PREDICTION, not a causal or
  treatment-specific effect of age.
* A literal single-group ("treatment arm") filter makes y constant -> complete separation -> the
  fitted probability degenerates to 1 (Groups=1) or 0 (Groups=2) at every age; such estimates are
  statistically uninformative, hence excluded from the answer (see 4c).
* Target is binarized by convention: PR = response, SD + PD = no response.
* Primary estimate is unpenalized MLE (canonical logistic regression). The sklearn default L2 (C=1)
  shrinks the coefficients and shifts p(65) slightly - reported as sensitivity only, not the answer.
* 41 trailing blank rows are formatting artifacts, not patients; one whitespace cell in Age -> NaN.
* No scaling of Age (raw years, prediction evaluated at 65), intercept included, no splines, no
  AUC/ROC, no cross-validation, no adjustment for ECOG-PS/Child-Pugh - all outside the fixed scope.
